FIX SCENE-BLOCK COLLECTOR (L1-7): fragment call sites dropped the slot index and block number

Init_Scene_Objects' level<8 path (body @0x430de8, shared with Ghidra's duplicate
Init_Track_Objects) walks 192 recorded camera strips and collects the wanted
scenery block numbers ([strip+0x1d]>>24) into the 14-slot local_4c array, then
decrunches them. When a NEW block is found, the code scans local_4c for a free
(-1) slot and jumps into the split-off fragment FUN_00430d0e (patch 365) which
performs the store:

  430ebe: mov edi,[ebp-0x48]     ; scan blocks[0]
  430ec1: mov esi,edx            ; esi = 0xe (sentinel: no slot yet)
  430ec7: cmp edi,-1
  430eca: jne 0x430cf8           ; scan loop: found -> 0x430ed0, exhausted -> 0x430d0e
  430ed0: mov esi,edx            ; ESI = FOUND FREE-SLOT INDEX
  430ed2: jmp 0x430d0e           ; fragment head: if (esi != 0xe) blocks[esi] = EBX
                                 ; EBX = the new block number, live since [strip+0x1d]>>24

Patch 365 reconstructed the fragment's parameters but passed (esi=0xe, ebx=-1)
at both entry call sites ("compile-time facts") and the stale unaff_ESI at the
fragment's self-recursion: with esi==0xe the fragment SKIPS the store, so no
block was ever collected -- Init_Scene_Objects returned with local_4c all -1,
loaded nothing, and left num_scene_objects/active_block_numbers at the previous
level's values. Visible result: the whole L6 attract-entry scenery layer
(overpass/mall walls, ~620 OT prims, depth buckets 1536-7167) missing for the
first ~150 cf until Update_Scene_Objects streamed the blocks in (ref-vs-our fb
diff 253013/307200 px at cf4, healing to 0 by cf150). L8+ was never affected
(sequential loader path @0x430d94). Measured after fix: identical inputs
(camstrip 0x6800, strip_data 0x7c2cd8) now produce ref's exact block set
{22,23,25,26,0,2,-1,17,18,19,20,21,24,1} / counts {31,29,15,2,...}.

The correct arguments, verified against the asm: slot index = scan offset>>2
(mov esi,edx @0x430ed0), block number = the live EBX (iVar6/iVar3/unaff_EBX).
The scan must therefore use a scratch variable (iVar4/iVar2, both dead after
the dedup loop) instead of clobbering the block number.

Also NOT touched here: patch 575's sliding-base chain walk in the duplicate
Init_Track_Objects -- measured today (L6 init, identical inputs): ref's
recorded_strips_ match the FIXED +0x1c refetch semantics (loop-back target is
0x430e22 = the edx refetch, so the add edx,4 is loop-dead), i.e. the live
Init_Scene_Objects copy is correct as-is; Init_Track_Objects has no C caller.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -21626,7 +21626,9 @@
     iVar5 = 0;
     while( true ) {
       if (iVar4 == -1) {
-        FUN_00430d0e(param_1,_blocks,_curv,unaff_ESI,unaff_EBX);
+        /* asm 0x430ed0: mov esi,edx = the found free-slot index, NOT the stale/0xe search
+           sentinel -- the recursion must store the new block (unaff_EBX) into that slot. */
+        FUN_00430d0e(param_1,_blocks,_curv,iVar5 >> 2,unaff_EBX);
         return;
       }
       unaff_ESI = 0xe;
@@ -21735,15 +21737,20 @@
         iVar4 = iVar4 + 4;
       }
       if (iVar5 == 0xe) {
+        /* asm 0x430ebe-0x430ed2: the free-slot scan keeps the NEW block number live in EBX
+           (iVar6 here) and jumps into the fragment with ESI = the found slot index (mov esi,edx
+           @0x430ed0); esi==0xe only on scan exhaustion (jge @0x430cff). Passing (0xe,-1) skipped
+           the store for every collected block -> L1-7 entry scenery empty. Scan with iVar4 (dead
+           after the dedup loop) so iVar6 survives to the call. */
         iVar1 = 0;
-        iVar6 = local_4c[0];
+        iVar4 = local_4c[0];
         while( true ) {
-          if (iVar6 == -1) {
-            FUN_00430d0e(iVar2,local_4c,iVar3,0xe,-1);  /* esi=search idx==0xe, ebx=iVar6==-1, [ebp-0x10]=iVar3 */
+          if (iVar4 == -1) {
+            FUN_00430d0e(iVar2,local_4c,iVar3,iVar1 >> 2,iVar6);
             return;
           }
           if (0x37 < iVar1 + 4) break;
-          iVar6 = *(int *)((int)local_4c + iVar1 + 4);
+          iVar4 = *(int *)((int)local_4c + iVar1 + 4);
           iVar1 = iVar1 + 4;
         }
       }
@@ -21831,15 +21838,18 @@
         iVar2 = iVar2 + 4;
       }
       if (iVar5 == 0xe) {
+        /* same slot/block-arg fix as Init_Scene_Objects (this is Ghidra's duplicate decompile
+           of the same 0x430de8 body; no C caller, kept consistent): scan with iVar2 (dead after
+           the dedup loop) so the block number iVar3 survives to the call. */
         iVar1 = 0;
-        iVar3 = aiStack_4c[0];
+        iVar2 = aiStack_4c[0];
         while( true ) {
-          if (iVar3 == -1) {
-            FUN_00430d0e(iVar4,aiStack_4c,iStack_14,0xe,-1);  /* esi=search idx==0xe, ebx=iVar3==-1, [ebp-0x10]=iStack_14 */
+          if (iVar2 == -1) {
+            FUN_00430d0e(iVar4,aiStack_4c,iStack_14,iVar1 >> 2,iVar3);
             return;
           }
           if (0x37 < iVar1 + 4) break;
-          iVar3 = *(int *)((int)aiStack_4c + iVar1 + 4);
+          iVar2 = *(int *)((int)aiStack_4c + iVar1 + 4);
           iVar1 = iVar1 + 4;
         }
       }
